#: app/templates/base/faq.html:20
msgid "Myeline is an AI-powered document intelligence assistant. You index your own sources (PDFs, RSS feeds, web pages, cloud files) and query them in natural language — as if you were talking to a colleague who has read everything.<br><br>Document indexing and semantic search run on our servers in France. For generating answers, Myeline uses the <strong>Mistral AI API</strong> — a French provider, EU-hosted — only your question and a few relevant excerpts are transmitted, never your full documents. Mistral AI contractually commits to not training its models on API data. Your data never leaves the European Union."
msgstr "Myeline is an AI-powered document intelligence assistant. You index your own sources (PDFs, RSS feeds, web pages, cloud files) and query them in natural language — as if you were talking to a colleague who has read everything.<br><br>Document indexing and semantic search run on our servers in France. For generating answers, Myeline uses the Google Gemini API — only your question and a few relevant excerpts are transmitted, never your full documents. Google contractually commits to not training its models on API data."

#: app/templates/base/faq.html:28
msgid "How does smart search work?"
msgstr "How does smart search work?"

#: app/templates/base/faq.html:33
#, python-format
msgid "The search is based on a technology called RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation):<ol><li><strong>Embedding (100%% local)</strong> — Your question is converted into a mathematical fingerprint and compared against all your indexed documents and sources. This step runs entirely on our servers in France — nothing leaves.</li><li><strong>Retrieval (100%% local)</strong> — The most relevant excerpts are selected automatically from your indexed content.</li><li><strong>Synthesis (Mistral AI API)</strong> — Your question and the selected excerpts (a few hundred words at most, not your full documents) are sent to the Mistral AI API (France, EU-hosted) to generate a cited, structured answer. Mistral commits by contract to not using API data to train its models.</li></ol>Your full documents never leave our infrastructure. Only short excerpts — the ones strictly needed to answer your question — are transmitted, and they stay within the European Union."
msgstr "The search is based on a technology called RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation):<ol><li><strong>Embedding (100%% local)</strong> — Your question is converted into a mathematical fingerprint and compared against all your indexed documents and sources. This step runs entirely on our servers in France — nothing leaves.</li><li><strong>Retrieval (100%% local)</strong> — The most relevant excerpts are selected automatically from your indexed content.</li><li><strong>Synthesis (Gemini API)</strong> — Your question and the selected excerpts (a few hundred words at most, not your full documents) are sent to the Google Gemini API to generate a cited, structured answer. Google commits by contract to not using API data to train its models.</li></ol>Your full documents never leave our infrastructure. Only short excerpts — the ones strictly needed to answer your question — are transmitted."

